   "text": {
    "L1": "A habitat is the place where a living thing lives and gets food, water, shelter and suitable conditions.",
    "L2": "A feature that helps an organism survive in its habitat is called an adaptation.",
    "L3": "Here is a myth: an animal changes its body on purpose to fit a place.",
    "L4": "That is not true. Adaptations develop over a very long time, across many generations.",
    "L5": "In a hot desert, a camel's long legs keep its body away from hot sand, and padded feet do not sink into sand.",
    "L6": "A cactus has spines instead of broad leaves, a thick fleshy stem that stores water, and a waxy coat that reduces water loss.",
    "L7": "Different habitats need different features: a yak has long thick hair for cold mountains, while a fish has gills, fins and a streamlined body for water.",
    "L8": "Now choose the cactus feature that helps reduce water loss."
   },
